simple loop was O(n),
but what is NESTED LOOP?

    for (int first:numbers) {           //the runtime complexity is O(n^2)
        for(int second:numbers){
            System.out.println(first + "," + second);
        }
    }

Note: How many execution we have?
      for each element we execute n times, we have n element
      so we execute n*n times!
      O(n^2)

Note: REMEMBER AS GOLD RULE
      we use "*" when we have nested cost
      we use "+" when they are separate execution

---------------------------------

    public void log(int[] numbers, int[] names) {   //O(n^3)

        for (int first:numbers) {                   //O(n)
            for(int second:numbers){                //O(n)
                for(int third:numbers){             //O(n)
                    System.out.println(first + "," + second + "," + third);
                }
            }
        }
    }

Note: we have nested O(n), so we use multiply
      O(n*n*n) = O(n^3)

---------------------------------

    public void log(int[] numbers, int[] names) {   //O(n^2)

        for (int first:numbers) {           //O(n)
            System.out.println(first);
        }

        for (int first:numbers) {           //O(n^2)
            for(int second:numbers){
                System.out.println(first + "," + second);
            }
        }
    }


Note: in big O notation, we just use the big term (it's big O)
      due to simplicity, we remove the smaller parts
      THE BIG O WANT TO SHOW THE "ORDER" OF FUNCTION

      O(n+n^2) = O(n^2)
      O(n+n^2+n^3) = O(n^3)